ID: vr-38
Title: Independent live FaceMesh and eye colors

Status: DONE
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/37
Milestone: Pick the FaceMesh wire and mechanical eye colors independently without regenerating speech.
Dependencies: vr-33, vr-37

Purpose:
The owner wants hex entry and a built-in color selector for both the FaceMesh
and its eyes. Preserve the current cyan/red default, selected glow structures
and fast audio-clocked renderer; no new model, dependency or automatic storage.

Tasks:
[x] Read the existing renderer, controls, qualification and ownership contracts.
[x] Add independent native color swatches, validated hex entry and reset.
[x] Apply uniforms live to FaceMesh only, including its matching hair.
[x] Qualify colors, validation/recovery, retained views/audio/defaults and cost.
[x] Update guide, book, brief/index and causal ledger; owned continuity follows.
[x] Prepare issue/Project reconciliation; source publication is recorded separately.

Acceptance criteria:
Each swatch opens the installed browser's built-in color selector. Hex entry
accepts #RRGGBB/#RGB, optional hash and either case; invalid input is visibly
reported and keeps the last valid render. Picker and hex stay synchronized.
Mesh and eye color are independent; eye geometry, glow choices and occlusion
remain intact. Black is supported; bright hot centers retain pale highlights.
Only FaceMesh and its optional matching wire hair change. Claire, FaceDot,
UniformPolygons and robot retain their colors. Reset/reload restores the
original exact renderer defaults. Switching views retains valid colors in RAM.
Live changes do not regenerate/seek/restart speech, build/upload geometry,
recompile shaders or introduce a timer, network call or durable preference.
No automatic device activation, user/sibling app interference or audible test.
README hero/default-closed section and existing media/releases stay unchanged.

